From: Pass 31 audit session <arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: Add the Loom concurrency-model job to CI (P31-02)

Context. Pass 31 wired nros-core for Loom: the crate's synchronization
primitives (the AlignedU64/AlignedBool reservation flags and indices, and Arc)
now resolve to loom's instrumented versions when the optional `loom` feature
is enabled, and crates/nros-core/tests/loom.rs runs the REAL
RingBuffer/Producer/Consumer protocol under loom::model (bounded
interleavings: two-message handoff, capacity-1 guard wraparound with a
guard-held preemption point, reservation/commit visibility). Feature is off by
default; native builds, Miri and the offline pipeline are unchanged.

What remains is EXECUTION. Loom requires the loom crate from crates.io
(unavailable in the offline audit sandbox), so the models must run in real CI.
modifying .github/workflows/ci.yml requires the `workflows` scope, which the
app token lacks (same limitation that kept F-20 and F-29 as staged patches).

This patch adds one self-contained job. It is a hard gate by design: loom
explores executions of the same unsafe SPSC core the safety case rests on, so
a failing loom run MUST fail the pipeline — do not add continue-on-error.
The models are bounded and complete in seconds; no timeout tuning needed.

Apply with:  git apply docs/audit/P31-02-ci-loom-job.patch
Then push with a token that has the `workflows` scope.
---
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -95,6 +95,22 @@ jobs:
       - name: Miri on nros-types
         run: cargo miri test -p nros-types --lib
 
+  loom-gate:
+    name: Concurrency model gate (Loom, hard)
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    env:
+      # Loom prunes provably-equivalent interleavings; the checkpoint bound
+      # only guards against runaway exploration, not correctness of a verdict.
+      LOOM_MAX_PREEMPTIONS: "4"
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+        with:
+          fetch-depth: 0
+      - name: Loom on nros-core SPSC protocol
+        run: cargo test -p nros-core --features loom --test loom --release
+
   nros-init-golden:
     name: nros init generates a buildable NROS project
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
